# =========================================================================
# llm/mod — LLM inference via hoosh.
#
# Parity oracle: rust-old/src/llm/mod.rs
#
# **The oracle's mod.rs is a `pub use` facade over the hoosh crate and cannot
# survive the port.** hoosh in Cyrius is a BINARY — no `dist/`, no `[lib]`
# stanza — so it is consumed as a **remote HTTP seam**, not linked. There is no
# crate to re-export from, so every `pub use hoosh::…` line necessarily
# evaporates. The reference for the seam is `thoth/src/hoosh.cyr`.
#
# What the re-exports were actually providing, measured rather than assumed
# (the port plan's "~20 zero-consumer re-exports" is wrong — 11 have real
# consumers, all of them in groups that land later):
#
#   Data types the seam defines locally — ProviderType (25 refs), Message (19),
#   Role (9), InferenceRequest (2), and HooshClient (10) as the seam client
#   itself. These belong to llm_hoosh.
#
#   Subsystems with no client-side equivalent over an HTTP seam — AuditChain
#   (36 refs), ResponseCache (10), CostTracker (10), llm_metrics (4),
#   cache_key (2), LlmProvider (2). hoosh implements these server-side
#   (`hoosh/src/lib/{audit,cache,budget,metrics,dlp}.cyr`) and does not expose
#   them over the wire. **Every consumer is in orchestrator (M5) or server
#   (M6)**, so whether agnosai reimplements them locally or drops them is an
#   M5/M6 decision, not an M3 one. AuditChain is the load-bearing case: 36
#   references across 11 server/orchestrator files, and it is the tamper-evident
#   audit trail, so it needs a deliberate call rather than a default.
#
#   Genuinely zero-consumer, safe to drop: TokenBudget, TokenPool, CacheConfig,
#   CompactionResult, ContextCompactor, TokenCounter, ModelPricing,
#   ProviderCostRecord, ClassificationLevel, DlpConfig, DlpScanner, HooshError,
#   ModelInfo, TokenUsage, RateLimitRegistry, AuditEntry, InferenceResponse
#   (llm-internal only), and the four Tool* types.
#
# Also corrected: the port plan lists `genai.rs` among llm's zero-consumer
# files. There is no `src/llm/genai.rs` — it is `src/telemetry/genai.rs`, it is
# declared by `telemetry/mod.rs:13`, and it therefore belongs to M9.
# `inference_queue.rs` IS llm's, is gated on the `majra` feature, and has no
# consumer outside its own module. It defers with that feature, alongside the
# other non-default-build exclusions listed in docs/development/roadmap.md
# ("What v2.0.0 is").
#
# Include order is a dependency constraint (Cyrius resolution is single-pass):
# llm_hoosh's error text is classified by llm_retry's `agnosai_is_retryable`,
# and both use core_json's field helpers, so `src/core/mod.cyr` must precede this
# hub. src/main.cyr does that.
# =========================================================================

include "src/llm/router.cyr"
include "src/llm/retry.cyr"
include "src/llm/hoosh.cyr"
